#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:7
#: 9a2063ab92de46fcb3a8f8e60e5ca998
msgid "This wiki page describes how a `VIO tracking camera <https://www.intelrealsense.com/visual-inertial-tracking-case-study/>`__ such as the `Intel RealSense T265 <https://www.intelrealsense.com/tracking-camera-t265/>`__ can be used with ROS to facilitate non-GPS flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:10
#: 5f23ec482a074f4390e939fad1fa3ecd
msgid "Explanation for some parts of the system will be kept short for the sake of brevity. More in-depth discussion can be found in the following blog posts `part 1 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/integration-of-ardupilot-and-vio-tracking-camera-part-1-getting-started-with-the-intel-realsense-t265-on-rasberry-pi-3b/43162>`__, `part 2 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/integration-of-ardupilot-and-vio-tracking-camera-part-2-complete-installation-and-indoor-non-gps-flights/43405>`__, `part 3 <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/integration-of-ardupilot-and-vio-tracking-camera-part-3-indoor-autonomous-flights-and-performance-tests/43626>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:13
#: 8e466d5bdae84d7eae80c711a90a7adc
msgid "Video"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:19
#: 19dbce38708f44cfa67c653333d93360
msgid "Hardware Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:20
#: 26a9aac1ab8348e29f2ababef401d35c
msgid "Sensor: `Intel RealSense Tracking Camera T265 <https://www.intelrealsense.com/tracking-camera-t265/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:21
#: f729dff8b29f4b69859830a70393c4e2
msgid "Companion computer: `Raspberry Pi 3 Model B <https://www.raspberrypi.org/products/raspberry-pi-3-model-b/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:24
#: fd4c2e04a3484bfe86b6c56e79c0f908
msgid "Depends on what you need from the T265, the companion computer should have USB2 (**pose** data only) or USB3 (**pose** + **image** data). For localization and navigation, we only need to capture pose data, so RPi 3B is sufficient for the task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:27
#: cce47eaff3724d00a78194eaeeeadfb4
msgid "System Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:32
#: 2911d78a902e44698ef95775c09f8b38
msgid "The position data obtained from ``realsense-ros`` node will be processed by ``vision_to_mavros`` node and send to ``mavros`` node via the topic ``/mavros/vision_pose/pose``. ``mavros`` will take care of the ENU - NED frames transformation and send it to ArduPilot through MAVLink."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:35
#: 34a88584be5740079bb67e593d5f9207
msgid "Install ``librealsense``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:38
#: ed93b793d8ea4c49b415956dd0778bbb
msgid "The Realsense T265 is supported via `librealsense <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense>`__ on Windows and Linux. Installation process varies widely for different systems. Refer to `the official github page <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense>`__ for instructions on specific system, such as `Jetson <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/blob/master/doc/installation_jetson.md>`__, `Odroid <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/blob/master/doc/installation_odroid.md>`__, `Windows <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/blob/master/doc/installation_windows.md>`__, `Raspbian <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/blob/master/doc/installation_raspbian.md>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:40
#: 10cfdb1d28d04462b0c89439dd19573b
msgid "The following steps are intended for Ubuntu Linux. Since no Debian package is available for RPi, ``librealsense`` must be built from source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:42
#: 4dbb309473ea44ab96efd7a28701af35
msgid "**Install OS** (if you have not done so): `Ubuntu MATE 16.04 LTS <https://ubuntu-mate.org/blog/ubuntu-mate-xenial-final-release/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:43
#: 9c38a17025f34d8a823c3dd9bdaaeb63
msgid "**Increase swap size**: RPi does not have enough RAM to compile the SDK, hence swap size needs to be increased. Swap size of 2048 (2GB) seems to work well, but you can go with less."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:66
#: 3799be4d259d443badbfcfdca8956b97
msgid "**Clone librealsense repo and compile SDK**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:107
#: 4de23c19c22c44bb98b5a2267db76e5a
msgid "**Test that librealsense is installed correctly**: The easiest way is to plug in the T265 and play with the `examples <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/tree/master/examples>`__ and `tools <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/tree/master/tools>`__ included in the SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:109
#: f8958b7e391c405b91c269c6ef90eff2
msgid "If you have a monitor plugged in, you can open `Intel Realsense Viewer <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/tree/master/tools/realsense-viewer>`__ by typing in into the terminal: ``realsense-viewer``. If the T265 is connected, the device will be available on the left panel. Click on the slider to start the device and switch to 3D view. Move the T265 around and you should see its trajectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:110
#: c2cd373aa3cc4dec91c7c2cd79b27c66
msgid "If no monitor is connected, other demos can also be launched from the terminal, for example ``rs-pose``, ``rs-pose-predict``, ``rs-capture`` etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:112
#: 643e55ccf24a42fdab99cf18820e67ac
msgid "**Test pyrealsense2 python wrapper**: If you enabled building Python wrapper (``BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS`` flag), the compiled library is located in the build folder: ``~/librealsense/build/wrappers/python``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:114
#: 49203e2be23a4a53b7a7ef97339aded0
msgid "Update the ``PYTHONPATH`` environment variable to add the path to the ``pyrealsense`` library: ``export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:/usr/local/lib``. Alternatively, copy the build output (``librealsense2.so`` and ``pyrealsense2.so`` files, located in ``~/librealsense/build/``) next to your script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:115
#: 4e03892973d24059958679b809ffd492
msgid "The basic examples provided by Intel can be found in the folder ``~/librealsense/wrappers/python/example``. Run it with Python3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:127
#: c76d9bde91114fd288b97b4b36fc4fe0
msgid "The RPi 3B with USB2 cannot handle the image streams. Trying to display the fisheye images might crash the application."
msgstr ""

