msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:178
#: 987446949f7545d78f0e510458171415
msgid "Modify parameters according to your T265 camera's orientation: The default parameters are set for a **front-facing camera**. In the launch file ``t265_tf_to_mavros.launch``, modify params ``roll_cam``, ``pitch_cam``, ``yaw_cam``, ``gamma_world`` from the list of values or with your own values corresponding to your setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:181
#: d9edab965de54be3a7b973c5f48ae436
msgid "There is a `known issue <https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/issues/4080>`__ about inconsistent yaw angle for **down facing** orientation and some workarounds have been discussed. As of this writing, here is what seems to work: the camera needs to be slightly tilted (i.e. not completely flat out) when it starts streaming poses (launching ``realsense-ros`` or calling ``librealsense``’s API to invoke pose data. Otherwise, the yaw angle of the world coordinates might be randomly initialized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:184
#: d6cc2a71262d43fe895ea674b9eac7d2
msgid "Configure ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:186
#: 7f8f7e8ac2f54a498944f554c2bb2542
msgid "Connect to the flight controller with a ground station (i.e. Mission Planner) and check that the following parameters are set as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:188
#: cc35183e35564ab08e4ccc58766f2eb3
msgid "`AHRS_EKF_TYPE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ahrs-ekf-type>`__ = 2 (the default) to use EKF2 (as of this writing, EKF3 is not supported for handling external navigation data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:189
#: 1931e414a4374a16b3edeaafed5e28a0
msgid "`EK2_ENABLE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ek2-enable>`__ = 1 (the default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:190
#: fdbf62bddb514b9ebb6008b2064ab148
msgid "`EK3_ENABLE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ek3-enable>`__ = 0 (the default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:191
#: 64d769bd5539441783d34bf00bb805de
msgid "`GPS_TYPE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#gps-type>`__ = 0 to disable the GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:192
#: aa9e210d83d24ad5b3b17835236cbd74
msgid "`EK2_GPS_TYPE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ek2-gps-type>`__ = 3 to disable the EKF’s use of the GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:193
#: 06c8054c8f5f4474b038b790d4ec946b
msgid "`EK2_POSNE_M_NSE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ek2-posne-m-nse-gps-horizontal-position-measurement-noise-m>`__ = 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:194
#: 4998a87fe38a4a558489cdbd24343495
msgid "`EK2_VELD_M_NSE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ek2-veld-m-nse-gps-vertical-velocity-measurement-noise-m-s>`__ = 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:195
#: 722e07e7295042c59879ed8d41010c9c
msgid "`EK2_VELNE_M_NSE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#ek2-velne-m-nse-gps-horizontal-velocity-measurement-noise-m-s>`__ = 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:196
#: 13cf0de7dbf24108af61c27d61cfb82d
msgid ":ref:`COMPASS_ENABLE<copter:COMPASS_ENABLE>` = 0,  `COMPASS_USE <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#compass-use-use-compass-for-yaw>`__ = 0, `COMPASS_USE2 <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#compass-use2>`__ = 0, `COMPASS_USE3 <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#compass-use3>`__ = 0 to disable the EKF’s use of the compass and instead rely on the heading from external navigation data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:198
#: 98c2db6456274ecca144b13d69de39f6
msgid "After the parameters are modified, reboot the flight controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:201
#: e41b0d1f84af41e29ab7c556346da9ea
msgid "Verify that all ROS nodes are working"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:203
#: 5a63691b533242218b9151cf161cc8d7
msgid "There are 3 ROS nodes running in this setup: ``realsense-ros``, ``mavros`` and ``vision_to_mavros``. Launch in 3 separated terminals on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:205
#: 4e3b3070e69f4bb7b9b1816e64affe60
msgid "``realsense-ros`` node: ``roslaunch realsense2_camera rs_t265.launch``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:207
#: 6bbd0799007049dda0c071dda06e4cc0
msgid "The topic ``/camera/odom/sample/`` and ``/tf`` should be published at 200Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:209
#: 3264db96e9c449458ede00269d4b8624
msgid "``mavros`` node: ``roslaunch mavros apm.launch`` (with ``fcu_url`` and other parameters in ``apm.launch`` modified to your setup)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:211
#: 66434da41c464e3186c9e25af8b4c6fb
msgid "``rostopic echo /mavros/state`` should show that FCU is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:212
#: 4c6c704a6d734fbcad8fb8de84752612
msgid "``rostopic echo /mavros/vision_pose/pose`` is not published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:214
#: bb4d497b0a244a508e8ece7ad8e17953
msgid "``vision_to_mavros`` node: ``roslaunch vision_to_mavros t265_tf_to_mavros.launch``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:216
#: 1ea919f795a745ce83d1fe9521274b57
msgid "``rostopic echo /mavros/vision_pose/pose`` should now show pose data from the T265."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:217
#: 171dd48075ee4afa853dd0f4f8cf09b2
msgid "``rostopic hz /mavros/vision_pose/pose`` should show that the topic is being published at 30Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:219
#: 32209e7da72a493abb194f1cc7e4000b
msgid "To verify that ArduPilot is receiving ``VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE`` on Mission Planner: press ``Ctrl+F`` and click on “Mavlink Inspector”, you should be able to see data coming in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:224
#: a61f8fa760b74a0991aeff8042e86a96
msgid "Once all of the nodes can run successfully, next time you can launch all of them at once with ``roslaunch vision_to_mavros t265_all_nodes.launch``, which will launch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:226
#: 28dc009bf68345c7af31b20de88045b4
msgid "``rs_t265.launch``, as originally provided by ``realsense-ros``, no modification needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:228
#: fbfeb201200745de877b9b700c6b0821
msgid "``apm.launch``, modified with your own configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:230
#: 6bf4ab0f4c354a1ab9585f147640834f
msgid "``t265_tf_to_mavros.launch`` with parameters according to your T265’s orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:233
#: 3c7732d2d8954706b637335ed25ab8da
msgid "Ground Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:235
#: 4677c94894ce4074bb0ecaab4eeaefad
msgid "After power on, launch all of the ROS nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:237
#: 3421c1eedfd247618c532e753fd64238
msgid "Generally (but not always), once ``mavros`` is running and the FCU starts receiving ``VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE`` message, you will see the messages “GPS Glitch” and “GPS Glitch cleared” confirming that the external localization data is being recognized by the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:239
#: a4912c0041e648d2a3df710521c8b3c0
msgid "Now you need to tell the EKF where the vehicle is in the world (i.e. **set EKF home**), otherwise incoming data will not be fused. To do this, you need to send the MAVLink messages `SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN>`__ and `SET_HOME_POSITION <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_HOME_POSITION>`__. There are a number of options for this to be done:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:241
#: e582e36c23db4bb7adb71cb205a0bb4f
msgid "**Use Mission Planner**: Right-click on any point on the map > ``Set Home Here`` > ``Set EKF Origin Here``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:246
#: b32e139f3652425caf43b93c68700aab
msgid "**Use code**: to send the required messages to the FCU through MAVLink. In Python, you can use this script `set_origin.py <https://github.com/anbello/aruco_gridboard/blob/master/script/set_origin.py>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:248
#: ecde13ddd24341b78359932ca0203ae4
msgid "Install ``pymavlink``: Follow the instructions `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/pymavlink#installation>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:250
#: 3d44a5096ddb4e83998f06453bc0899d
msgid "Run the script: ``rosrun vision_to_mavros set_origin.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:252
#: 5d24167f2e804f2fb493ef091fea854c
msgid "You should see a quadcopter icon appear on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:254
#: f72593ab14954433a93e4dee5b7a4170
msgid "Pick-up the vehicle and walk it around, check that the vehicle’s position movements are shown on the map. The trajectory of the vehicle on the map should reflect the real movements without too much distortion or overshoot. Below is an example of walking in a 2m x 2m square."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:260
#: ff28ba1b43d649638407554d8ad2511b
msgid "Flight Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:262
#: 1ab661d429a940d5896a54680f70df69
msgid "For your first flight: - Takeoff in Stabilize or Alt-Hold, check that the vehicle is stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:265
#: bd5df626cab7404ba845e91c73727611
msgid "Move the vehicle around and observe the position on Mission Planner as well as ``rviz`` to see if tracking is stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:267
#: c7ecc08c8258449b959a22a483abc523
msgid "Switch to Loiter, but always ready to switch back to Stabilize/Alt-Hold if anything goes awry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:269
#: b4f97cafa19a4ad4a525f28d000d4650
msgid "Otherwise, the vehicle should hover stably and able to keep its position. Move the vehicle back and forth 2-3 meters, verify the scale (easier to view on ``rviz``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:271
#: d0d3f4ed81434e658174300c0daf3273
msgid "Move the vehicle around (translate, rotate) at varying speed, always ready to switch back to Stabilize/Alt-Hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:273
#: 8ba0b060d2f448c29962111dd6400458
msgid "If everything works as expected, next time you can arm and take-off in Loiter mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:277
#: 53a74da0cc554cc0bea12666914b7c0d
msgid "Always confirm that position feedback is running ok before switching to Loiter mode. Look out for the working boundary in your environment, i.e. where tracking might be lost due to lack of features, fast or rotation movement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:286
#: 32a3b33edcd049719931cbbece550e71
msgid "Data Logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:288
#: 67df46a856d24f759975588e7fc12a87
msgid "Visual odometry information will appear in the ``VISO`` dataflash log messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-vio-tracking-camera.rst:291
#: 9b415de288fa479fbb4c569d4759b0ed
msgid "References"
msgstr ""

